.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL> void \fBcsmp::FiniteElementPolicy\fP< dim, CELL >::CoordinateMatrix () const"

.PP
initialises the nodes x dim matrix XY stored in the connected finite element class Writes the Elements node coordinates into a matrix of rows=nodes, columns=spatial dimensions\&. The coordinate matrix is internally initialized for connected \fBFiniteElement\fP subclass\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
During the visitation of an element the coordinate matrix is initialized only once, if the method is called without argument\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
for efficiency this method checks an element id in the connected finite element against that of the current element that it is called by\&. If they are the same, nothing is done\&. Thus, YOU MUST SET THE ELEMENT ID for this method to have an effect\&. 
.RE
.PP

