.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL> template<class Var> void \fBcsmp::FiniteElementPolicy\fP< dim, CELL >::PropertyValueAt (const \fBcsmp::Index\fP & idx, const std::vector< double > & xyz, Var & var) const"

.PP
interpolates node property values to the point of interest (in global coordinates); 
.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
costly for isoparametric elements
.RE
.PP
Interpolates property value to a point within the element as specified using physical coordinates\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
If this method is used on an element with a local coordinate system the point in local coordinates has to be found iteratively\&. This is a much slower procedure than direct interpolation\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
If variable is an element property, method will simply return this value\&. 
.RE
.PP

